WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:03.470
- We have seen the heart
breaking images from Australia.

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:05.290
Everybody's been probably
keeping up with that

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:08.230
and where the fires have
just devastated that country.

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:11.830
18 million acres burned,
3000 homes were destroyed,

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:14.470
and probably the most
shocking statistic of all,

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:17.930
is up to a billion animals
may have lost their lives,

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:21.140
which is so sad, look at, oh my gosh.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:22.830
I've watched the news and like all of you,

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.640
my heart breaks for
the people of Australia

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.190
but where there is tragedy

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:28.180
there are always people that are helping

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:30.020
and including the Irwin family.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:31.640
They operate the Australia Zoo

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:34.290
which has taken in tens
of thousands of animals,

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:35.750
you might remember I had Bindi, Robert

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:36.930
and Terri on last year.

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:39.620
And so I reached out to them
for an update on their efforts

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:42.160
and how we here in the
U.S. could help in any way.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:43.760
So they're joining us from Australia.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:45.740
Might be a little bit of a
delay, it's gonna be great.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:47.914
Hey everyone, what's going on?

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:50.910
(applause)

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:54.900
Hi, (screams) they're so cute.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.770
Tell us who you have here.

00:00:56.770 --> 00:00:58.170
- They are so adorable.

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:00.340
We've got two little flying foxes,

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:01.992
also known as fruit bats.

00:01:01.992 --> 00:01:02.977
- Or sky puppies.

00:01:02.977 --> 00:01:04.017
- Or sky puppies.

00:01:04.017 --> 00:01:05.910
They basically are little sky puppies.

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:08.190
And these little ones are orphans.

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:09.960
They are absolutely adorable.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:12.373
And we've seen hundreds
and hundreds of fruit bats

00:01:12.373 --> 00:01:15.180
that've been taken up to
our state of Queensland,

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:16.950
that need rehabilitation

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:20.060
because of the fires that
are happening down south.

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:22.590
- So they were too little
to escape the fires.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:24.020
So their mommas flew away,

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:25.670
but then they were stuck.

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:29.520
We've gotten about 700
fruit bats up here so far.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:30.650
- Wow.

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:32.370
So some of the animals you're caring for

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:33.940
are extremely vulnerable, right?

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:35.680
Not just the fruit bats, right?

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:37.110
- Absolutely.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:38.980
We have so many different species

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:42.009
of Australian wildlife
coming through our doors.

00:01:42.009 --> 00:01:45.000
We have koalas that are being treated.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.703
The poor koalas get stuck
in the eucalyptus trees

00:01:47.703 --> 00:01:51.570
and the eucalyptus trees
just catch fire instantly.

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:53.200
They almost explode.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.410
And the koalas have nowhere to go.

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:56.420
It's unbelievable.

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:59.601
So thankfully here at the
Australia Zoo Wildlife Hospital,

00:01:59.601 --> 00:02:03.200
we have now treated over 90,000 sick,

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.900
injured and orphaned animals.

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:05.733
- [Kelly] Way to go.

00:02:05.733 --> 00:02:06.706
- And we're doing everything we can

00:02:06.706 --> 00:02:08.843
to treat every single animal
(applause)

00:02:08.843 --> 00:02:10.275
that comes through our doors.

00:02:10.275 --> 00:02:11.108
It's incredibly important.

00:02:11.108 --> 00:02:13.300
- So we obviously now
what y'all are doing,

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.510
you're, you know, providing
miracles over there

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:16.380
for these animals.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.660
But I know there are a
lot of people in the U.S.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:19.493
that want to help,

00:02:19.493 --> 00:02:21.920
so what's the best way
we can get involved.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:22.870
Like, where can we spend money,

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:24.801
or where can people in
Australia give time.

00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:26.680
What are all those options?

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:27.513
- Sure.

00:02:27.513 --> 00:02:30.100
So it's really helpful, if
you want to help wildlife,

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:32.430
to donate to Wildlife Warriors

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:34.360
at wildlifewarriors.org.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:36.660
We are a charity in the United States,

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:39.590
which means it's a tax
deductible donation,

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:41.840
and then the funds are
transferred to Australia

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.790
to help in this emergency time.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:45.050
So thank you so much.

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:48.510
That way we can send
care packages of medicine

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:51.050
and food to the front line of the fire.

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:54.210
We can help people who are
dealing with transporting animals

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:55.310
up here for help.

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:57.490
And we can get our teams of veterinarians

00:02:57.490 --> 00:02:59.575
and technicians down to assist as well.

00:02:59.575 --> 00:03:02.243
- [Kelly] Well, thank you so much.

00:03:02.243 --> 00:03:03.076
(applause)

00:03:03.076 --> 00:03:05.875
- Like, just on the behalf of humanity,

00:03:05.875 --> 00:03:09.110
thank you so much for just
doing so much for these animals.

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:10.620
We know that your family loves animals

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.570
and just what you're
doing is so important,

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:14.460
it's so inspiring to all of us.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.310
So we have links on our website

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:18.230
for ways people at home can help.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:21.520
Just be sure to go to
kellyclarksonshow.com for more info.

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:22.890
And Terri, Bindi and Robert,

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:24.770
thank you all so much
again for just what you do.

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:25.603
Good luck,

00:03:25.603 --> 00:03:27.572
and thank you so much
for joining us again.

00:03:27.572 --> 00:03:28.632
(applause)

00:03:28.632 --> 00:03:29.671
- Thank you for being Wildlife Warriors.

00:03:29.671 --> 00:03:30.548
- [Kelly] Have a good 2020.

00:03:30.548 --> 00:03:31.381
- Thanks Kelly.

00:03:31.381 --> 00:03:32.214
- Thank you so much.

00:03:32.214 --> 00:03:33.103
We love you.

